5BSD import status
==================

Upstream:  nghttp2 1.70.0, https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2
Archive:   https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2/releases/download/v1.70.0/nghttp2-1.70.0.tar.xz
SHA256:    e05cb1388eaca3830aded4ccf20044b6e1ac1a61411dcca11b0437c4285c8bc2
           (equal to the www/libnghttp2 port's distinfo)
License:   COPYING (MIT).  lib/sfparse.c also carries the MIT notice of
           Bjoern Hoehrmann's UTF-8 decoder; files from ngtcp2, nghttp3
           and sfparse are MIT under their contributors' notices.

Trimmed to the library, as the port's --enable-lib-only
(tools/build/protobuf/trim.py): lib/ and its public headers.  Not
imported: the applications, tests, examples, bindings, documentation,
the bundled third-party code (mruby, munit, llhttp, ...) and the build
system.  The port's Makefile.in patch only limits the build to lib/ and
has no source counterpart.

Local changes: none.  lib/libnghttp2/config.h (the four macros the
library sources test) and lib/libnghttp2/nghttp2/nghttp2ver.h (the
upstream template with version 1.70.0, 0x014600) replace configure.

Built by lib/libnghttp2 as the private library libprivatenghttp2.so.14
(libtool -version-info 43:5:29).  Installed licence:
/usr/share/licenses/nghttp2.
